## DESCRIPTION
## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Hypothesis tests)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Institution(The College of Idaho)
## Author(R Cruz, L Danielson, J Guild)
## Level(1)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('The Basic Practice of Statistics')
## AuthorText1('David Moore')
## EditionText1('5e')
## Section1('14')
## Problem1('')
## KEYWORDS('statistics', 'inference', 'confidence interval')
## Updated: 2010/10

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',   'PGML.pl',
    'parserPopUp.pl',  'parserRadioButtons.pl',
    'randomPerson.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

$per = randomPerson();
$n   = random(8,     23);
$p   = random(0.005, 0.15, 0.001);

$dd1 = DropDown([ 'Yes', 'No' ], $p < 0.05 ? 0 : 1);
$dd2 = DropDown([ 'Yes', 'No' ], $p < 0.1  ? 0 : 1);

$rb = RadioButtons(
    [ [
        'The \(P\)-value is less than \(\alpha\).',
        '\(\alpha = 0.05\)',
        '\(\alpha\) is small.',
        'The \(P\)-value is greater than \(\alpha\)',
    ] ],
    0,
    labels => 'ABC'
);

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML
[$per] thinks a certain potato chip maker is putting fewer chips in their
regular bags of chips. From a random sample of [$n] bags of potato chips 
[$per->they] calculated a [`p`]-value of [$p] for the sample.

a)  At a 5% level of significance, is there evidence that [$per] [$per->are]
    correct? [_]{$dd1}

b)  At a 10% level of significance, is there evidence that [$per->they] [$per->are] correct?
    [_]{$dd2}

c)  In a statistical test of hypotheses, we say that the data are statistically
    significant at level [`\alpha`] if [_]{$rb}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) Since the [`P`]-value is [@$p < 0.05 ? 'smaller' : 'greater' @] than 0.05, there is 
    *[@ $p<0.05 ? '' : 'not' @] evidence* than [$per] [$per->are] correct. 

b) Since the [`P`]-value is [@$p < 0.1 ? 'smaller' : 'greater' @] than 0.05, there is 
    *[@ $p<0.1 ? '' : 'not' @] evidence* than [$per] [$per->are] correct. 

c) A test is *significantly significant* only if the [`P`]-value is smaller than [`\alpha`]. 
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
